# debian -- Debian 13 / Ubuntu 24.04 or newer, and what says ID_LIKE=debian
# (Ubuntu on WSL 2 too). One file per package family, the same eight keys
# in each (contract 3): the manager, its install line for a human, the
# name the docs use, and the five package groups bootstrap.sh
# --list-packages prints after OS and site branching (contract 1). The
# packages check row and spark uninstall read the same file through
# lib/spark/packages.py. Every name here is credited in CREDITS.md.
PM=apt
PM_INSTALL=sudo apt-get install -y
PM_TARGET=Debian 13 / Ubuntu 24.04 or newer
# core -- the AI: SITE_SHELL=off installs only these (+ PKG_AI for vulkan)
PKG_CORE=git curl ca-certificates python3
# llama.cpp's Ubuntu build needs OpenMP; Debian's base lacks it
PKG_ENGINE=libgomp1
# the vulkan build only (ai_build: a GPU in sysfs, or SITE_AI_BUILD=vulkan)
PKG_AI=libvulkan1 mesa-vulkan-drivers
# the shell layer -- SITE_SHELL=on (spark shell on): tmux, the font's
# unzip + fc-cache, a tmux-256color terminfo
PKG_SHELL=bash tmux unzip fontconfig ncurses-bin
# the shell's daily tools
PKG_CLI=bat eza fzf zoxide ripgrep fd-find jq btop
